Dear Robert,

Please find the Q1 2019 inspection status for the ATU-100. We are currently operating under the updated piping inspection plan QSCP-IP-ATU100 Rev 3, which rationalized the CMLs to 150 across 18 lines. This plan implements RBI intervals of 3 years for Class 1 sour gas, regenerator overhead, and rich amine, and 6 years for the remaining lines.

Our current baseline remains the full-unit survey conducted by Larkhall NDE Services Inc. as detailed in LNDE-RPT-20160118-004-R0. We are monitoring these against the established retirement thicknesses to ensure compliance with site rules.

Regards,  Jennifer Walsh

